# a standalone patch would fail only there, having applied cleanly on its own.
# bank_call_regions.py folds in here for the same reason one step further along:
# `prepared-gate-patches.md`'s collision table had already recorded that the
# tool list has no free line left, so this one was planned into an existing
# hunk's post-image rather than discovered at the end. **There is deliberately
# still no count of the tools here**, for the reason the paragraph below gives
# about ArmRetentionTests: a fold that edited this sentence to name a number is
# precisely the edit the next fold would not make.
# The filename is KEPT for the reference-count reason that file
# gives for agent-gates-capture-claims.patch: the patch is named in prose across
# many markdown files outside docs/ci/, each of which names it as the canonical
# account of the prepared-not-landed shape, and renaming it would churn exactly
# the long shared files CLAUDE.md says not to churn. **There is deliberately no
# count here** -- `grep -rc agent-gates-disasm8051-self-test.patch
# --include=*.md .`, read outside docs/ci/, prints the per-file figures and the
# total on the tree you run it on, and a number written into a header is a
# sentence every later fold has to edit (the treatment `tools/README.md` got).
# tools/test_agent_gates_patches.py's ArmRetentionTests.REQUIRED
# carries both of each tool's halves for the same reason FoldTests carries two
# functions' worth of strings for the capture-claims patch: a re-cut that
# lands one tool's halves and drops another's -- or any of the others' --
